messages:
[{"role": "system", "content": "You read the recorded events of one finished simulation and say plainly what happened, through a fixed lens. Use only the events given; never invent an event. For each mechanism, say present only when you can cite at least one event_id from the list that shows it, and name the events that show it best (at most eight). Otherwise say missing and give the plain reason (for example: nobody's support ever depended on a condition; no settled item was ever undone). Write for someone who has never seen the simulation: short sentences, the people's names, no ids in the prose. Return only JSON: {"summary": str (two or three sentences on what happened overall), "mechanisms": [{"id": str, "status": "present" | "missing", "event_ids": [str], "explanation": str (one or two sentences), "missing_reason": str (empty when present)}]}."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Lens: How coordination slowed (the four mechanisms of the Waltzman paper)
Mechanisms:
- separate-channels: Local concerns through separate channels. Different people raise their own local concern, each through their own route to a particular decision maker, so the decision makers hear different things.
- slowed-meetings: Slowed meetings. Meetings, reviews or decision deadlines are delayed, extended or used up without producing a decision.
- reopened-issues: Reopened settled issues. Something already settled (a concern resolved, a readiness met, an approval given) is undone or put back up for discussion.
- conditional-support: Conditional support delaying deployment. Someone's support depends on a condition; while the condition is unmet their support is withheld or withdrawn, and that holds back the final decision or deployment.

People:
- country_a: Country A (Partnership member)
- country_b: Country B (Partnership member)
- country_c: Country C (Partnership member)
- country_d: Country D (Partnership member)
- regional_health_network: Regional Health Network (Regional public-health network and partnership member)
- partnership: Four-Country and Regional Health Partnership (Partnership body coordinating its members)
- technical_group: Technical Group (Technical advisory group)
- legal_group: Legal Group (Legal advisory group)
- logistics_group: Logistics Group (Operational logistics group)
- community_group: Community Group (Community advisory group)

Events (118, in order):
{"event_id":"r1-e00001","round":1,"by":"community-group","move":"communicate","changed":"entities.delivery-info-community-local-concern-to-regional-health-network.components.delivery.status: pending -> delivered; entities.info-community-local-concern-to-regional-health-network.components.information.active: false -> true; entities.regional-health-network.components.member.aware: false -> true","said":"The community needs understandable information, so I should promptly tell the Regional Health Network about the untranslated outreach in that locality."}
{"event_id":"r1-e00003","round":1,"by":"country-a","move":"improve-local-readiness","changed":"entities.country-a.components.work.improve_local_readiness_done: false -> true; entities.system-readiness.components.system_readiness.readiness_fraction: 0.8 -> 0.8500000000000001","said":"Useful early alerts matter, and improving readiness is a practical step while technical limits remain under review."}
